            <ArticleTitle>Acute coronary syndrome: new advances and nursing strategies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Glycoprotein IIb/IIIa receptor inhibitors are the newest therapy for acute coronary syndrome (ACS). This article reviews the pathophysiology of ACS, the role of glycoprotein IIb/IIIa receptor inhibitors, and nursing care for patients undergoing this therapy and coronary interventions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
